content"><p>Given two strings <code>s</code> and <code>t</code> of lengths =
<code>m</code> and <code>n</code> respectively, return <em>the <strong>mini=
mum window</strong></em> <span data-keyword=3D"substring-nonempty" class=3D=
" cursor-pointer relative text-dark-blue-s text-sm"><button type=3D"button"=
 aria-haspopup=3D"dialog" aria-expanded=3D"false" aria-controls=3D"radix-_r=
_t_" data-state=3D"closed" class=3D""><strong><em>substring</em></strong></=
button></span><em> of </em><code>s</code><em> such that every character in =
</em><code>t</code><em> (<strong>including duplicates</strong>) is included=
 in the window</em>. If there is no such substring, return <em>the empty st=
ring </em><code>""</code>.</p>

<p>The testcases will be generated such that the answer is <strong>unique</=
strong>.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> s =3D "ADOBECODEBANC", t =3D "ABC"
<strong>Output:</strong> "BANC"
<strong>Explanation:</strong> The minimum window substring "BANC" includes =
'A', 'B', and 'C' from string t.
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 2:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> s =3D "a", t =3D "a"
<strong>Output:</strong> "a"
<strong>Explanation:</strong> The entire string s is the minimum window.
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 3:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> s =3D "a", t =3D "aa"
<strong>Output:</strong> ""
<strong>Explanation:</strong> Both 'a's from t must be included in the wind=
ow.
Since the largest window of s only has one 'a', return empty string.
</pre>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li><code>m =3D=3D s.length</code></li>
	<li><code>n =3D=3D t.length</code></li>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D m, n &lt;=3D 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>
	<li><code>s</code> and <code>t</code> consist of uppercase and lowercase E=
nglish letters.</li>
</ul>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Follow up:</strong> Could you find an algorithm that runs in <co=
de>O(m + n)</code> time?</p>
